Otherwise it is lower bounded by 
    \begin{equation*}
        \max_{\theta \in [0,1]^d} R(T,\theta) \ge C'_4 T
    \end{equation*}
    with $C_4,C'_4 > 0$ universal constants.

Then the regret of TS is lower bounded by
    \begin{align*}
        R(T,\theta) &\ge  {\Delta \over p_\Delta}(1 - (1-p_\Delta)^{T})  \text{     with } 
    p_{\Delta} = {1 \over m m !} \left[\ln \left({1 \over 1 - \Delta} \right)\right]^{m}. 
    \end{align*}
